---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Navbar from '../components/Navbar.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';

const title = 'Terms & Conditions | Cinematic Photo Editor';
const description = 'Read the terms and conditions for using Cinematic Photo, the free client-side online cinematic photo editor.';
const lastUpdated = 'August 7, 2026';
---

<Layout title={title} description={description} path="/terms-and-conditions/">
	<Navbar />
	<main class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-20 sm:px-6">
		<span class="mb-4 block font-mono text-xs tracking-wide text-mute">TERMS &amp; CONDITIONS</span>
		<h1 class="font-sans text-3xl font-semibold tracking-[-0.03em] text-ink sm:text-4xl">
			Terms &amp; Conditions
		</h1>
		<p class="mt-3 font-mono text-xs text-mute">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>

		<div class="mt-8 flex flex-col gap-6 text-base leading-7 text-body">
			<p>
				These Terms &amp; Conditions ("Terms") govern your use of Cinematic Photo at
				cinematicphoto.com (the "Service"), operated by Cinematic Photo ("we", "us", "our"). By
				using the Service, you agree to these Terms. If you do not agree, please do not use the
				Service.
			</p>

			<h2 class="font-sans text-xl font-semibold tracking-[-0.02em] text-ink">Use of the Service</h2>
			<p>
				Cinematic Photo is provided free of charge for personal and commercial use. The Service
				applies color grading, film grain, letterboxing, and related visual effects to images you
				choose to open in your browser. All processing happens locally on your device; we do not
				receive or store the images you edit.
			</p>

			<h2 class="font-sans text-xl font-semibold tracking-[-0.02em] text-ink">Your content and ownership</h2>
			<p>
				You retain full ownership of any photo you edit with the Service. Because images are
				never transmitted to us, we make no claim to, and have no access to, your content. You
				are responsible for ensuring you have the necessary rights to any image you edit and for
				how you use the resulting output.
			</p>

			<h2 class="font-sans text-xl font-semibold tracking-[-0.02em] text-ink">Acceptable use</h2>
			<p>
				You agree not to use the Service to process or generate content that is unlawful,
				infringes on the rights of others, or violates applicable law. You also agree not to
				attempt to disrupt, reverse engineer for malicious purposes, or interfere with the normal
				operation of the Service.
			</p>

			<h2 class="font-sans text-xl font-semibold tracking-[-0.02em] text-ink">Digital products and purchases</h2>
			<p>
				We sell certain digital products, such as PNG template packs, as one-time purchases.
				These purchases are processed entirely by our reseller, Dodo Payments (Dodo Payments Inc.),
				which acts as the merchant of record for the transaction, handles billing, sales tax, and
				customer support for the order, and is bound by its own
				<a href="https://dodopayments.com/terms-of-use" class="text-ink underline decoration-hairline-strong underline-offset-2 hover:decoration-ink" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">terms of use</a>.
				Purchasing a digital product grants you a non-exclusive, non-transferable license to use
				the files in your own personal or commercial projects; you may not resell, redistribute,
				or repackage the files themselves. Because digital files are delivered instantly on
				purchase, all sales are final once a file has been downloaded, except where required
				otherwise by applicable law.
			</p>

			<h2 class="font-sans text-xl font-semibold tracking-[-0.02em] text-ink">No warranty</h2>
			<p>
				The Service is provided "as is" and "as available," without warranties of any kind,
				whether express or implied, including but not limited to warranties of merchantability,
				fitness for a particular purpose, or non-infringement. We do not guarantee that the
				Service will be uninterrupted, error-free, or compatible with every browser or device.
			</p>

			<h2 class="font-sans text-xl font-semibold tracking-[-0.02em] text-ink">Limitation of liability</h2>
			<p>
				To the fullest extent permitted by law, Cinematic Photo shall not be liable for any
				indirect, incidental, special, consequential, or punitive damages, or any loss of data or
				output, arising from or related to your use of the Service.
			</p>

			<h2 class="font-sans text-xl font-semibold tracking-[-0.02em] text-ink">Changes to these Terms</h2>
			<p>
				We may update these Terms from time to time. Material changes will be reflected by an
				updated "Last updated" date on this page. Continued use of the Service after changes take
				effect constitutes acceptance of the revised Terms.
			</p>

			<h2 class="font-sans text-xl font-semibold tracking-[-0.02em] text-ink">Contact us</h2>
			<p>
				Questions about these Terms can be sent via our <a href="/contact-us" class="text-ink underline decoration-hairline-strong underline-offset-2 hover:decoration-ink">Contact Us</a> page.
			</p>
		</div>
	</main>
	<Footer />
</Layout>
